# Build context for oci/Dockerfile (see `bun run build:image`). Everything the
# image does not need stays out — the runtime stage copies only
# pi-vs-claude-code-vendor/ and the generated oci/.build/NOTICE.
.git
.github
.claude
.gitnexus
.swarm
# The live-E2E scratch tree. Holds fake-box fixtures that carry their own `.env`
# files, so it must go out with `.swarm` rather than lean on the credential
# patterns at the bottom — those are non-recursive and would miss every one of
# them. Nothing COPYs it.
.sandbox
node_modules
# Docker patterns are not recursive: without this a nested dependency tree (e.g.
# pi-vs-claude-code-vendor/node_modules) would be copied into the image WITHOUT
# being part of the swept tree.
**/node_modules
_bmad-output
docs
tests
# The exedev builder's scratch space (per-run `run-*` dirs holding a ~1.6 GB
# docker archive each) lives INSIDE the build context; without this, one
# uncleanly-died run ships its debris to the builder on every later build.
# Deliberately NOT the whole oci/.build: oci/Dockerfile COPYs oci/.build/NOTICE.
oci/.build/exedev
# `src`, `scripts` and `cli-anything` USED TO BE EXCLUDED HERE, and DF1.10
# removed the exclusions rather than negating them with `!`: oci/exedev's
# engine builder stage COPYs all three (the phase engine it compiles, and
# cli-anything's team-lead driver), and a `!`-negation of a path a sibling rule
# still matches is the kind of ordering puzzle nobody re-reads correctly. They
# are context-only for oci/Dockerfile, which COPYs neither — a wider context
# costs upload time, not image bytes.
#
# WHAT STILL PROTECTS THEM: `**/node_modules` below keeps every nested
# dependency tree out, and the credential patterns at the bottom are recursive
# for exactly this reason. Adding a tree to the context is not adding it to an
# image; the INV-IBOX-1 scan reads the built filesystem either way.
# `**/`-prefixed since #217's bundle (round-4 item): docker patterns are NOT
# recursive, so a bare `*.log` matched only the repo root while a stray
# `scripts/debug.log` rode a COPY'd subtree into the CONTEXT (and, under a
# dirty tree, into the buildId walk — the two exclusion sets must move
# together, and build-exedev-image.ts mirrors these two in contextFilesUnder).
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
# Defence in depth: nothing COPYs these, but they should not be in the context
# either — the credential scan (INV-5) is the backstop, not the first line.
# `**/`-prefixed for the same reason `**/node_modules` is above: docker patterns
# are NOT recursive, so a bare `.env` matches only the repo root and a nested
# `app/.env` sails into the build context. Neither COPY in oci/Dockerfile
# (`pi-vs-claude-code-vendor/`, `oci/.build/NOTICE`) matches any of these.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
